WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:07.680
Call them what you will, be it myths, urban
legends, ghost tales or just fool yarns; the

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:10.720
fact is we’ve all heard at least one.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Traditionally, stories like that were just
shared around a campfire, but nowadays they

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.160
have ended up spreading far and wide across
internet message boards and creepy threads.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.640
Everything ranging from unsolved missing persons&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.920
cases actually being the&nbsp;
result of alien abductions,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.200
to haunted videos carrying an unforgiving
curse or some missing, unaired episode of

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.240
popular tv shows that had somehow been unearthed
by an online sleuth.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.920
We’re always quick to share these ideas,
these stories, but deep down a part of us

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.320
knows that there’s no truth to them.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.440
Urban myths are speculation that someone has
turned into a tale of terror, for nothing

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.040
more than to give some quick scares to whoever
they tell it to.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:59.200
But then that person passes that tale on to
someone else, and suddenly the story had become

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.600
a widespread legend with no discernible point
of origin.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.960
Sure, they might still be fictional, but through
sharing these stories, we as humans bring

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.240
them to life.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.440
Not literally, of course,&nbsp;
that would be outlandish.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.800
After all, when was the last time you heard
of a fictional story becoming reality…?

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.240
Growing up with exposure and unfiltered access
to the internet in the late 2000s, Paul Jacobs

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.600
and his friends had been fascinated with – and
admittedly, pretty terrified by – the notorious

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.760
legend of the Slender Man.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.040
It began as whisperings in an online forum,
a story that was intentionally designed to

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.040
be a modern day urban myth.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:42.640
And just like so many others before it, the
myth spread.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:48.160
What had started as a forum post became unnerving
photoshopped images of a tall, faceless figure

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:54.320
in a suit lurking in the woods, next an indie
video game, and even a real world tragedy.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.360
Given how young he was at the time – still
being in high school – Paul and a few others

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.400
had bought into the Slender Man myth wholesale.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.840
He believed it to be real, this towering,
expressionless boogeyman.The more he learned

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.280
about this malevolent creature, every story,
blog post or creepy YouTube video made about

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.280
Slender Man, only added more and more to his
legend, and kept young Paul awake at night,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.760
afraid that every noise outside his bedroom
window was the faceless horror.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.720
Of course, if you take away that belief, the
possibility an urban legend might be true,

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.880
then it simply loses its power.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.640
It’s that potential, that maybe, toeing
the line between fantasy and reality, that

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.560
can allow these stories to go on and incite
fear forever.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.880
But that wasn’t the case for the Slender
Man story, and the craze for it quickly died

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.840
down after it was debunked numerous times
over, casting it permanently back into the

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.280
realm of fiction.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:56.160
But the profound effect the legend had on
Paul at a young age ended up informing his

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:56.880
future.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:01.920
As he grew older, his past fear of certain
stories became a keen interest in how these

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.600
tales could influence people.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.840
Could any story have that same impact, or
only those that walked the line between being

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.040
fictional and maybe being true?

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.360
Did these urban legends become more real to
people because of their subject matter, or

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:21.040
did human beings give them that power to transcend
the constraints of fiction just by believing

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:21.760
in them?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.040
As Paul got older, he began to study the truth
behind certain urban legends, attempting to

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.440
trace them back to their origins.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.560
Some were often inspired by real events, but
with specific details that had gradually been

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.960
altered from the original story the more and
more people passed it around.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.240
Ghost stories seemed to be the most changeable,
but with some roots in the real world.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.720
A person might have died a hundred years ago,
and the story of them haunting their old home

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.760
or final resting place would start to circulate.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.280
Then, shortly after, another similar story
might emerge, and the two would overlap.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.560
Whoever was telling each story might have
added or omitted certain details, or combined

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:07.760
elements of more than one tale, until what
was left being passed around was neither the

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.440
first story nor the second, but a hybrid of
different versions from different storytellers.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:18.480
There was one legend that Paul felt drawn
to more than others, and it was a rather obscure

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.000
one to say the least.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:25.440
During his self-conducted research into stories
of this nature, he learned about a tale that

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.640
told of an ancient sect called the Daevites.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.760
According to legends – some that dated so
far back they preceded almost all recorded

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:38.480
history – these Daevites were a callous
and cruel civilization.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.760
They had emerged from a book, so the story
went, and sought only to wage war on other

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.480
cultures and enslave their enemies.

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:51.600
But Paul also uncovered one detail of the
story that intrigued him more than any other.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:57.120
It referred to something known as the ‘Eternal
Text’, and was regarded as some kind of

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.160
deity or figure of worship by the Daevites.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.880
The legends stated that this Text had helped
create the book that they had emerged from.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:09.440
Of course, this all sounded like highly fictitious
nonsense to Paul Jacobs.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.080
He knew that things of such nature didn’t
exist in the real world, they were only part

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.120
of stories.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.600
But he had noticed that this particular story
seemed to have passed its way through the

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.480
ages.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.880
Searching further, Paul had uncovered the
works of an obscure author from the United

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.320
States, who had only a few works that were
known about during the 1940s and 50s.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.800
Even then, most of his stories weren’t widely
published, only a few shorter pieces making

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.480
it into a magazine that had long since stopped
being printed.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.560
This writer had died in 1957, having never
seen his career in fiction come to much fruition.

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:49.040
But, despite his short-lived career and being
considered a somewhat sub-par author at the

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:54.800
time, the writer’s work had garnered its
own little cult following online, mostly comprised

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.160
of amateur authors.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.960
It was through them that Paul managed to obtain
some scanned copies of the anonymous writer’s

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:06.400
stories, particularly some that he felt bore
a striking similarity to the Daevite legends

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.000
of the Eternal Text.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.920
One story in particular – written in a style
lifted directly from H.P.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:17.200
Lovecraft – was based on a supposed encounter
the writer claimed to have had with something

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.000
that closely resembled the Eternal Text.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.720
Paul also studied the writer’s own personal
journals that he had managed to recover scans

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.280
of.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.840
The entries from it seemed to imply that the
author came across what he called the ‘Written

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.840
God’ and that this compelled him to write
a fictional version of those events.

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:37.120
It was only after writing&nbsp;
about this new encounter,&nbsp;

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.440
that what he had depicted in his story seemed

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:43.120
to come true, exactly as he’d written them.

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:48.480
This led to a recursive process of the writer
creating these encounters, only for them to

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.800
occur, thus causing him to write about it
and then make it happen.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.600
The entire prospect not only confused and
bewildered Paul, but intrigued him further

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.480
as well.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:03.040
Although he had no way of confirming what
this writer had claimed was true, Paul believed

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.480
that on a smaller scale, the author had achieved
the same effect that occurs during the passing

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:09.920
down of urban legends.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:15.920
But the difference here was, that it had all
been done through himself, via a singular

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.360
person telling variations on the same story,&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.440
allowing it to continue&nbsp;
and perpetuate recursively.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.400
Of course, Paul didn’t actually believe
in this ‘Written God’ or ‘Eternal Text’,

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.400
those were all just part of the fiction.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.040
But he wanted to experiment further, and see&nbsp;

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:36.400
if he could achieve the same&nbsp;
process for himself.Taking

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.440
an empty notebook, Paul started to write the
first things that came to mind, basing a short

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.000
story off of the anonymous’ authors own
tale.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.520
He intentionally changed a few key details,
noting down things that weren’t in the original.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.320
“The Written God appeared behind me,”
he wrote, adding on a whim the line: “It

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.840
had no face.”

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.360
The whole intention of Paul’s experiment
was to pass his new version of the story on

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:04.080
to someone else, and then try to get them
to write it from memory.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:09.520
He wanted to observe if their mind would change
certain details subconsciously, or if they

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:13.040
would misremember elements when they retold
their new version.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:18.320
If enough people could spread the story around,
each time altering or adding new parts to

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.640
it, what effect could it have?

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.800
As he finished his rewritten version of the
author’s tale, attaching it to an email

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:30.560
to send to one of his fellow writers, Paul
was blissfully unaware of just what he’d

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:31.280
done.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:35.760
A heavy knocking rang out, somebody’s fist
pounding at the front door loud enough to

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:36.480
wake him.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:40.400
Bleary-eyed, Paul checked the alarm clock
next to his bed; it was the middle of the

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.040
night.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:46.640
Stumbling out of bed, he staggered his way
towards the repetitive noise, unsure who…

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.360
or what would be calling this late.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:53.520
Paul froze for a second, casting his mind
back to the story he had written earlier.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.920
Surely not, it couldn’t be, right?

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.920
It was just a story after all.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:02.560
But the author, he had described how the things
he’d written had come true.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.160
There it was, that possibility, that maybe…

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.360
what if it was behind the door right now?

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.680
Suddenly, something much heavier than a hand
bashed against the wooden surface of the front

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.920
door, causing it to fly open, the catch of
the lock being ripped out of the wall by the

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:19.200
force of the impact.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.520
A group of black-clad figures rushed in, one
of them tackling Paul to the ground before

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.440
he could even process what was happening.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:30.400
The weight of another person pinned him down
and kept him from moving despite his attempts

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.000
at struggling free.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.720
Then, the feeling of something sharp poked
at the exposed skin of Paul’s neck, a needle

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.920
filled with… he wasn’t sure, all he really
knew right now was how dizzy he was.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:46.880
Unable to stop himself from slipping away,
the sedative quickly put Paul back to sleep,

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:49.280
as the agents filed into his home.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:52.080
The floor he woke up on was freezing cold.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:56.800
Blinking his heavy eyelids until they opened
again, Paul did his best to stand.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.600
His head was still spinning, making it hard
to keep his feet still, and to make matters

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.400
worse, the room around him was hardly lit.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:08.560
Only a few low fluorescents dimly illuminated
the tiny space.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:14.080
“Mr. Jacobs,” a voice boomed over a crackly
intercom, the pitch lowered to distort it

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.840
further, “We need you to answer a few questions
for us.”

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:18.640
“What?”

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.400
Paul responded in confusion.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.360
“Where did you first learn about SCP-582?”

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:27.200
the voice questioned, barely giving Paul a
moment to think.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.240
“About what?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:30.582
What’s an SCP?” he asked back.

00:10:30.582 --> 00:10:33.440
“You wrote a story earlier today, correct?”

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.520
boomed the unseen speaker.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.600
Meekly, Paul nodded his head.

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:43.600
“We monitor online activity for any mentions
of SCP-582, or anything using any of its known

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.800
aliases.”

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:48.240
“You mean that Written God, Eternal Text
thing?”

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.120
Paul replied, catching on to what the voice
had been referring to.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:54.880
“I read about it in some stories by this
old author, he died ages ago, most of his

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.080
work is pretty niche, it’s actually hard
to track down-”

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.920
“Enough,” the voice interjected bluntly.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:03.200
“When did you specify SCP-582 would manifest?”

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:06.160
‘
“Manifest?” he raised an eyebrow, confused

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:06.800
again.

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:10.880
“It was just a story, that’s what I was
doing, I was examining stories and how they

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:12.880
change when they get passed on.”

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:14.560
“Mr. Jacobs.”

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:19.520
It sounded as though the voice had shifted,
still distorted but now calmer, more collected;

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.040
somebody else was speaking.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.880
“It’s important you answer our questions,
your life could very well be in danger.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:35.120
Now, do you remember when you wrote that SCP-582
– when it – was going to appear?”

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:37.920
“What do you mean ‘in danger’?”

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.360
Paul retorted in a panic.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.280
“Who the heck even are you people?”

00:11:41.280 --> 00:11:43.440
“Calm down, Mr. Jacobs.”

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.400
He looked down to see his hands were trembling,
suddenly aware of the sweat coating his forehead.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.920
Paul took a series of deep breaths, trying
to collect himself.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:52.160
“I…

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:57.680
I don’t remember,” he sighed, his voice
now shaking as much as the rest of him was.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.520
“What about a location?”

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:00.640
the voice pressed him.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.600
“Can you tell us where it’s going to appear?”

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:08.800
“I didn’t write a location either,”
Paul answered, “I just said it appeared…”

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:14.160
The words he had written earlier quickly came
crashing back into his head, almost like an

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.360
urgent warning.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:16.640
“Behind me…”

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:21.520
As he spoke, Paul could sense someone standing
near him, that same sensation you get when

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:25.760
you know another person is in the room, even
when you haven’t looked directly at them

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.240
yet.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:30.480
Paul tried to keep his head forward, only
tilting it slightly to the side, seeing something

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:33.120
dark looming just behind his shoulder.

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:37.440
He couldn’t rationalize any of what was
happening, too scared to turn all the way

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:38.240
around.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:43.120
Doing that would mean admitting all of this
was real, and not just some horrific nightmare…

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:45.120
not just a story.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:49.680
“We, uh,” for the first time, the voice
over the intercom sounded uneasy.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:53.440
“We think you need to turn around, Mr. Jacobs.”

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:58.560
Telling himself he’d wake up any second,
Paul rotated with his eyes screwed shut, snapping

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.480
them open once he was facing…

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.200
nothing.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:06.240
A blank space, lacking any expression and
all of the normal features was looming over

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.200
him with an empty, eyeless stare.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.480
It had no face, just like in Paul’s story.

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:16.800
He opened his mouth to let out a scream, only
for it to be interrupted by the crunching

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.520
sounds of neck bones twisting the wrong way.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:26.000
As Paul’s lifeless body dropped back down
to the cold floor, SCP-582 vanished just as

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:27.840
quickly as it had arrived.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.080
***
The thing about some anomalies is, you have

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.960
to be very careful about how you talk about
them.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:37.200
Not just because they could be listening in
and might hear you, but because what you say

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:40.640
about them might just have a nasty habit of
coming true.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:47.680
That’s the case with SCP-582, otherwise
known as its rather apt nickname ‘A Bundle

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:48.880
of Stories’.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:54.880
What’s so fitting about that title is its
accuracy, that’s all SCP-582 really is:

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.480
stories.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.440
But therein lies its true power.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:02.080
This entity has a way of&nbsp;
propagating and perpetuating&nbsp;

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.640
itself, continuously adapting and spreading

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.480
like a mutating virus.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:11.600
Except it doesn’t pass from person to person
as an illness, there are no symptoms.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.160
It transmits via stories.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:20.560
SCP-582 is subject to a process of passive
reality manipulation; it doesn’t necessarily

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:26.560
directly change the world around it, but can
itself be changed by certain factors.

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:32.160
What this means is, anything said or written
about this entity, even if pulled out of thin

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.800
air, a fictional account of its deeds…

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:37.040
all becomes real.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:42.640
Let’s say, for example, you told a story
about SCP-582 sneaking up behind a Foundation

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.800
researcher when his back was turned.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:49.760
Telling that story would cause those exact
events would be carried out in the real world.

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:53.920
When SCP-582 manifests, it&nbsp;
will do so in accordance&nbsp;

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.480
with any details given in a fictional account

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:02.000
about it; the same time, the same place on
Earth, it would appear in the exact form that

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.600
the tale specified.

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:08.880
If any of those details were omitted, or purposely
left vague, then the entity would still be

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:14.320
able to manifest, and would do so in a way
that fits the rest of the narrative, appearing

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:18.160
wherever and whenever it has an opportunity
to.

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:24.240
As far as the researchers at the SCP Foundation
can tell, the actual abilities of SCP-582

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.960
are usually left vague when people write about
it.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:33.040
One of the few consistencies is that the entity
can disappear and reappear at will, to any

00:15:33.040 --> 00:15:34.720
place or time.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:40.640
Another is that no method of harming or even
killing SCP-582 has ever worked, even if written

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:43.680
down as fiction in order to be made fact.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:48.160
Any other details or abilities that someone
assigns to the creature will, however, become

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:53.200
a permanent addition to its growing myth,
meaning it is able to perpetually increase

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:55.600
its power the more people write about it.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.960
On the rare occasion multiple different writers’
accounts of SCP-582 contradict each other,

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:07.280
or don’t fit into the entity’s own ‘canon’,
it can easily adapt to these contradictions.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:12.000
This usually results in conflicting information
having no effect on the Bundle of Stories,

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:16.320
or having so little impact that it is almost
like they didn’t happen at all.

00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:20.240
In short, if one author’s story doesn’t
quite match up with another’s, then the

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:26.480
effect these additions have to SCP-582 and
its ongoing story are lessened so that they

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:30.480
can all either logically occur, or be negated
completely.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:35.520
It is because of this adaptability, and that
it has been described by multiple sources,

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:40.000
that portrayals of SCP-582 tend to be generalized.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:44.480
This even extends down to its appearance;
it’s currently unknown what the entity’s

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.160
true form is, or if it even has one.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:53.520
However, the fact that it is usually depicted
as a deity or god, means that this Bundle

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:58.560
of Stories has been known to manifest as one
of several avatars.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:03.680
The most common of these appearances is that
of a humanoid being, standing well over six

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.720
feet tall.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:10.960
When manifesting as this particular form,
SCP-582 is dressed in thickly layered robes,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:14.800
made from burlap – or hessian – complete
with a hood.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:19.280
However, no face is visible underneath the
creature’s hood, and when presenting as

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:24.640
this avatar, it is often described as carrying
sacks of unknown contents, sometimes even

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.480
appearing to bleed heavily.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:32.320
There have been a number of other incarnations
of SCP-582 including a six-legged form that

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:37.760
is made out of pure molten tar and will attack
any nearby human beings on sight.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.200
This avatar would normally appear as being
fused with the first.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:46.240
In other instances, it has appeared as a plant
capable of producing both light and enough

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:50.480
radiation to kill anyone in its radius within
a few hours of exposure.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:55.600
Other times, it has been a vaguely human shaped
shadow, and even has one form that exists

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.680
within more than three dimensions.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:02.880
Due to this form existing on higher dimensions,
this made it impossible to properly perceive

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:08.000
with the naked eye, and resulted in the deaths
of anyone who looked even partially at it.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:13.040
Who knows, maybe at some point it has even
been described as a tall, slender figure in

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:20.000
a dark suit, with pale skin and a face with
its eyes, ears, nose, and mouth all missing?

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:24.000
Actually, it’s probably best that nobody
writes it down, we don’t want it becoming

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.920
real now, do we?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:31.840
The question is, how can you hope to contain
or even fight something that can be anything,

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:36.160
anywhere, and have any strength that someone
claims it has?

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:40.640
Well, just to be on the safe side, the Foundation
uses its own fictional narrative to keep the

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.000
entity contained.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:46.880
It is their hope that, by describing it as
powerless, it will turn the creature’s own

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:53.440
reality-altering properties against it, and
actually cause SCP-582 to lose its abilities.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:59.200
“What thoughts, if any, that flow through
that alien mind are not mine to know: It remains

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:04.720
silent and still within its chamber, entrenched
in the persistence of its own memory.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:11.040
It remains, but only as a shade of what it
was, its power spent, or at least come to

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:11.840
rest.”

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:17.760
So, remember, SCP-582 possesses no actual
consciousness or free will.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:22.880
Anything it has ever said or done is because
someone wrote that it would.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:27.280
And yes, we’re only saying that because
we don’t want to write that it’s broken

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:33.280
free from containment and is currently standing
behind you… if we did that, it might just

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:33.920
come true.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:39.440
Now go and check out “SCP-023 THE BLACK
SHUCK” for another anomalous entity that

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:43.360
has slipped its way into the zeitgeist of
mythology and legend.

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:47.200
Or if you’re looking for more monsters of
memetic madness, then why not get yourself

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:51.200
acquainted with “SCP-2440 THE SEALED KING”!

